// 'Return If(c, a, b)' returns AdvPL's If(): its parentheses hold a comma of
// their own. It is not 'return if c', the modifier -- xc took it so, and
// returned nothing (saulogm/advpl-excel, custom.excel.tlpp). 'return if
// lSkip' and 'return if (lSkip)' stay modifiers.
user function f(lOk, nDiv)
  if lOk
    return if(nDiv > 1, 2, 3)
  endif
return If( nDiv>Int(nDiv), Int(nDiv)+1, ;
  Int(nDiv) )

user function g(lSkip)
  return if lSkip
  return if (lSkip)
return 2
